    "title": "One injured after tree falls on victim in Troy - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Aaron Smith ,\n1 days ago\nTROY, N.Y. (WNYT) – One person was taken to the hospital after officials say a tree fell on them in Troy.\nRelated: 7-year-old hurt after being hit by car at Albany intersection\nAccording to officials with the City of Troy, it happened in the area of Spring Avenue and Kinloch Avenue.\nOfficials say the male victim, approximately 60-years-old, was walking out of his front door when a tree fell on him.\nRelated: Pedestrian dead after being struck in Albany\nThe victim was taken to Albany Medical Center with non-life-threatening injuries. Officials say he is conscious and alert.\n3",
    "summary": "TROY, N.Y. (WNYT) – One person was taken to the hospital after officials say a tree fell on them in Troy. Related: 7-year-old hurt after being hit by car at Albany intersection According to officials with the City of Troy, it happened in the area of Spring Avenue and Kinloch Avenue. Officials say the male victim, approximately 60-years-old, was walking out of his front door when a tree fell on him. Related: Pedestrian dead after being struck in Albany The victim was taken to Albany Medical Center with non-life-threatening injuries. Officials say he is conscious and alert.",
